rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All runtime-native workflows must comply with the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model, ensuring separation of concerns where the Runner orchestrates and workflows
    reason without assume repository structure or performing direct discovery.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision lifecycle (governance validation), preventing the conflation of observed
    patterns with approved architecture.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all new patterns must be created as 'supporting' by default
    to ensure they are validated through usage evidence before potential promotion
    to 'core'.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the merging or consolidation of patterns that exist in different
    architectural layers to preserve clarity between governance, execution, contracts,
    and reliability.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core status must be supported by strong, observable
    evidence from multiple sources or system contexts to maintain architectural stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Work as the authoritative source of planning state;
    generated artifacts like AEM and AID must derive their status from this registry.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces the use of a structured YAML schema for all architectural decisions
    to enable machine processing and consistent system-wide interpretation.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared workspace and are prohibited from
    duplicating global, runtime, or template governance structures.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the mandatory semantic contract for architecture artefacts, distinguishing
    between intent and state, and standardizing lifecycle terminology.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must maintain traceability by linking to
    at least one observed signal as evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the resolution model for conflicting rules, prioritizing Global
    Rules over Project Rules, and Project Rules over Prompt Rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop governance by requiring all system-proposed
    architectural decisions to be explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an
    architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Governance artifacts such as AEM and AID must summarize authoritative source
    data and must not be used to store primary planning or decision state.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded exclusively in Architecture Decision
    Records (ADR), which serve as the single source of truth for all derived representations.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory criteria including recurrence, system impact, reusability,
    and stability that a candidate signal must satisfy before promotion to a pattern.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR files before
    they can be reflected in the Architecture Evolution Map or other system artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage (e.g., DONE, NEXT, FUTURE) of any architecture item
    must be derived directly from its governance decision status.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) must remain consistent with and never
    contradict the decisions recorded in Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives rather
    than specific strategies or implementations to ensure long-term architectural
    stability.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
